1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Attached you will find scans of two obituaries published in Prague in Národní listy (issue 91 volume 79 from 1939-04-01 and issue 321 volume 61 - from 1921-11-22); more recent proves that Maryla Gross née Brettauer
2 CONC  was the wife of Mr. Bedřich Gross, and the older obituary of her brother-in-law shows the names of his siblings, including Bedřich. Bedřich and Maryla lived in Prague's Bubeneč villa district in a house designed by architect Frid
2 CONC rich Ehrman (https://www.ds.cz/cz/cesky-objekty-ds/cesky-praha-6-bubenec/cesky-charlese-de -gaulla-915- 27-praha-6 /). They both were very good golfers and their golf history was mapped by the Czech golf enthusiast and scholar Mr.
2 CONC  Prokop Sedlák. Bedřich Gross resigned from the position of Austrian Honorary Consul in Prague in 1936 due to the Phoenix insurance company scandal, which began with the death of Mr. Berliner; Bedřich Gross was one of the highest 
2 CONC representatives of the Czech branch of this company and also one of Mr. Berliner's closest collaborators. (Michal Šedivý, 2022)
