1 OCCU ABD Damberg, Alsace, France, Rabbi
1 TITL R'
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} R' Eliezer Katzenellenbogen (Eleazar Lazarus) of Alsace was born in 1700.
2 CONT
2 CONT He became A.B.D. in Bamberg in Bavaria and then A.B.D. in Hagenau n Alsace from 1755-1771.
2 CONT
2 CONT His wife was Jached, daughter of R' Samuel Helman A.B.D. of Metz (died 1766). They were of the Heilprin family and a distant relative of his mother Leah. Leah was the daughter of R' Eliezer Heilprin.  He was one those consulted ab
2 CONC out the Cleves divorce case, which involved his brother and his relative R' Israel Lipschutz. (See Lipschutz Family Pedigree - Chapter V1 - C).
2 CONT
2 CONT He wrote approbations to Chamesh Shitot LaRaMBan by Nachmanides, published Sultzbach 1762 and Chochmat Shlomo by Solomon Luria, published Sulzbach 1782.
2 CONT
2 CONT Novellae were left on the Talmud in manuscript. His responsa arrearwth those of his brother, R' Phineas, published in Frankfurt-on-Main 1857. In Ohr Hayashar there is a responsum of his to his brother R' Naftli, written in Hagenau
2 CONC  in 1766.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Source=
2 CONT
2 CONT The Unbroken Chain - Neil Rosenstein (1990) Volume 1, Chapter 11, page 101, G 8.2
2 CONT --------------------
