1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Israel Markovich Brodsky was born into a family of Jewish entrepreneur Meer shore, the great-grandson of Rabbi Sender (Alexander) Shor, who lived in the town of Zhovkva at the end of XVII century and was from the f
2 CONC amily of Tias shore. Meer shore moved to Zlatopol ' from the town of Brody and married the daughter of a local wealthy Jew. After the death of Meer Shor, Israel received the inheritance — 40 thousand rubles.<br/>
2 CONT Israel Brodsky started renting manufacture of sugar sugar factories, but due to lack of experience almost completely burned out, preserving however a small portion of their capital.<br/>
2 CONT Brodsky began to frequent in the factories of count A. A. Bobrinsky, learn, observing the work of artisans and agronomists.<br/>
2 CONT Its first refinery is 23-year-old Israel Brodsky was founded in 1846 in the village of Swan near Zlatopole, eight versts from the future station Shpola. His companion was a local landowner Petr Lopukhin. Companions purchased, havi
2 CONC ng fallen into decay Lebedinsky sugar factory and converted it into the sugar-refinery — refined sugar at that time was more profitable product.<br/>
2 CONT For eight years they were companions, and then production moved to full ownership Brodsky. Lebedinsky sugar factory increased its production volumes from 10 thousand pounds to 1 million pounds of refined sugar annually. In 1855, I
2 CONC srael Brodsky in zlatopil ' founded an orphanage for the poor elderly and donated to his estate in Bobrinetskii County, fifteen hundred acres of land, which gave more than 3 thousand rubles of annual income.<br/>
2 CONT Israel Brodsky also founded a sugar factory in Odessa, took a long-term lease Raigorodskii sugar factory. In 1860, Israel Brodsky moved to Odessa with his family — wife Chaya, four sons and three daughters. In December 1865, Brods
2 CONC ky filed a petition for reckoning it from the Odessa merchants in Kiev.<br/>
2 CONT In April 1870, Israel Brodsky was bought in Kiev at the hem mill, which was called by his name — the-mill Brodsky. In 1873, Israel Brodsky founded Aleksandrovskoe Association of sugar factories, the largest of the sugar trust in t
2 CONC he Russian Empire, which included 7 plants. In the future, the trust has added four more plants Koryukovka, Tomashpolskiy, Makharinsky and Voskresenskim under the guidance Brodsky was 13 sugar mills and 10 sugar and 3 refinery. Th
2 CONC e plant has more than 10 thousand people. Factories of the partnership was made at the time from 15 to 25 % of all domestic refined sugar. By 1913, when the heirs of Israel Markovic, the main capital of the Alexander partnership h
2 CONC as made fabulous at the time 20 million.<br/>
2 CONT Israel Brodsky was a lot of money spent on charity and construction.<br/>
2 CONT In 1885 the new Lukyanovka district of Kiev on a dedicated Brodsky money (150 thousand rubles) build a Jewish hospital with 100 beds. Treatment and medication in the hospital was free, not only for inpatients but also outpatients.
2 CONC <br/>
2 CONT Brodsky has also contributed more than 40 thousand rubles for the construction, equipment and maintenance of a vocational school for children from poor families.<br/>
2 CONT Brodsky died in September 1888. '''Family '''<br/>
2 CONT * Father Meer Shore, mother Miriam.
2 CONT * Brothers — Abraham, Selman, Isaac and Joseph.
2 CONT * Wife Haya.
2 CONT * four sons — Lazar, Lev, Solomon (suffered mental illness and was under the care of brothers).??.
2 CONT * three daughters.
