1 NAME Friedrich (Fritz) Karel /Gross/
2 GIVN Friedrich (Fritz) Karel
2 SURN Gross
2 _MARNM Gross
1 NAME Bedřich Karel //
2 GIVN Bedřich Karel
2 SURN Gross
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 9 MAR 1877
2 PLAC Modřany 52
2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://katalog.ahmp.cz/pragapublica/permalink?xid=2C16EFC2532745AEA160A220646D0248&scan=131#scan131
2 CONT
2 CONT Attached you will find scans of two obituaries published in Prague in Národní listy (issue 91 volume 79 from 1939-04-01 and issue 321 volume 61 - from 1921-11-22); more recent proves that Maryla Gross née Brettauer was the wife of
2 CONC  Mr. Bedřich Gross, and the older obituary of her brother-in-law shows the names of his siblings, including Bedřich. Bedřich and Maryla lived in Prague's Bubeneč villa district in a house designed by architect Fridrich Ehrman (htt
2 CONC ps://www.ds.cz/cz/cesky-objekty-ds/cesky-praha-6-bubenec/cesky-charlese-de -gaulla-915- 27-praha-6 /). They both were very good golfers and their golf history was mapped by the Czech golf enthusiast and scholar Mr. Prokop Sedlák. 
2 CONC Bedřich Gross resigned from the position of Austrian Honorary Consul in Prague in 1936 due to the Phoenix insurance company scandal, which began with the death of Mr. Berliner; Bedřich Gross was one of the highest representatives 
2 CONC of the Czech branch of this company and also one of Mr. Berliner's closest collaborators. (Michal Šedivý, 2022)
