1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Was the author of several essays and ''Yesh Manchilim''
2 CONT
2 CONT From Avrohom Marmorstein, mehadrin@aol.com Further sources from I D Feld’s thorough introduction to Yesh Manchilin, the autobiography of rabbi Pinchas Katzenelonbpgen of Boskovice grandfather of Rabbi Berish K of Hotzenplotz Rabbi
2 CONC  Horowitz of Dresden writes that Pinchas K died in Ansbach in 1767 Index of Kelilas Yofi (Dembitzer) reports 1755 [either of which would fit in with a grandson dying in 1833 A.M.] Pinchas K’s second marriage was in 1722 and Gabrie
2 CONC l K Markbreiter was his second son from that marriage (presumably born around 1725)  According to Feld, Berish Markbreit died 24th Tamuz 1833 at the age of 72 after serving as rabbi in Osoblaha for over 40 years
