1 NAME Naftali Hirsch /קצנלנבוגן/ A.B.D. Manheim
2 GIVN Naftali Hirsch
2 SURN קצנלנבוגן
2 NSFX A.B.D. Manheim
2 _MARNM Katzenellenbogen
2 NICK Naphtali Hirsch Katzenellenbogen
2 NICK Naftali Tzvi Hirsch Katzenellenbogen
1 NAME נפתלי הירש /קצנלנבוגן/
2 GIVN נפתלי הירש
2 SURN קצנלנבוגן
2 _MARNM קצנלנבוגן
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 23 FEB 1712
2 ADDR
3 CITY Schwabach
3 STAE Bavaria
3 CTRY Germany
1 DEAT
2 DATE 21 SEP 1800
2 ADDR
3 CITY Mannheim
3 STAE Baden-Württemberg
3 CTRY Germany
1 OCCU Rabbi
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} See "Unbroken Chain"  p. 110 
2 CONT
2 CONT Naftali Hirsch Katzenellenbogen of Schwabach, died 1800.  He was also called Hirsch Moyses.  He was born in Schwabach, where his father was the Av Beit Din (A.B.D.) He studied in his youth  under R. Jacob Cohen Popers of Frankfurt
2 CONC -on-Main, and later married his daughter, Frumet, as his first wife.
2 CONT
2 CONT At this time he published his "Toldot Adam" on the Talmud, from an old manuscript written by Moses ben Nachman (Nachmanides), published in Homburg 1740.  
2 CONT
2 CONT From 1741-63 he was ABD of Mergentheim, where he wrote approbations to:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. 2. 3. 4. 5. 6.
2 CONT
2 CONT After his first wife died in 1733, he married Merle, daughter of Ellen Oppenheim of Hamburg (died Brody, 1743) and Lieb Mochiah (father of Isaiah Berlin).  She died in 1804.
2 CONT
2 CONT After Mergentheim, he was elected Chief Rabbi of the Palatinate (Pfaltz or Kurpfalz) with his seat at Leimen, which he transferred ato Manheim in 1768.  There despite ill health, he was surrounded by many pupils.
2 CONT
2 CONT Naftali died in Manheim on September 21st, 1800, and left behind manuscripts housed in Oxford.
2 CONT
