1 NAME R' Benjamin Katzenellenbogen, Rosh Beth Din Krotoschin
1 NAME בנימין בן שאול // מקראטשין
2 GIVN בנימין בן שאול
2 SURN קצנאלנבוגן
2 NSFX מקראטשין
1 NAME ר' בנימין מקראטשין אב"ד סמטור
1 SEX M
1 DEAT
2 DATE 24 DEC 1788
2 ADDR
3 CITY Krotoszyn
3 STAE Greater Poland Voivodeship
3 CTRY Poland
1 OCCU
1 TITL R'
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} R' Benjamin Katzenellenbogen was a prominent author of the 18th century.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a pupil of Samuel Helman (of the Heilprin family) of Metz (died 1766). R' Benjamin became A.B.D. of Samter (Prussia) and then of Krotoschin, Krojanke and Gelnhausen.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the author of Or Chachamim, published in 1752,  Frankfurt-on-Oder;  Lev Chachamim published in 1773, Dyhernfurth;  and Menorat Zahav, including Or Olam, Or Chadash and Or Torah, published 1775, Dyhernfurth.
2 CONT
2 CONT Approbations were written to:
2 CONT * Pa-amonei Zahav by R' David Katz, son of R' Joseph Weiner, published Furth 1769; 
2 CONT * Chagorat Shmuel by R' Samuel son of R' Azriel, published Frankfurth-on-Oder 1772; 
2 CONT * Or Lisharim by R. Raphael, son of Jacob Jaffe, written in 1776, published Dyhernfurth 1778, and 
2 CONT * Torat Moshe by Moses Kaner, written in 1786, published in 1786.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Source=
2 CONT
2 CONT The Unbroken Chain - Neil Rosenstein (1990) Volume 1, Chapter 11, page 92-93, G 11.<br/>
2 CONT The Unbroken Chain - Neil Rosenstein (third edtion) Volume 1, page 34, G9.2
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT The Unbroken Chain (1990), Neil Rosenstein, 1990, page 17, G7
2 CONT
2 CONT R Benjamin Wolf of Krotoschin, mentioned in the Responsa Chinuch Beit Yehuda, written by R Hanoch, ABD Schneitach, published Frankfurt-on-Main in 1708.  He married the daughter of R Jacob son of R Ephraim Shor
