1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Helen Reinfrank was born Helene Feistmann on March 10, 1915 and grew up as the daughter of a Jewish family in Berlin. After massive reprisals by the Nazi state, all family members were forced to flee Germany. Helen
2 CONC e Feistmann lived in exile in London from January 1937 as a seamstress, often in material need, and was an important contemporary witness of the work of the Free German Kulturbund and possessed numerous documents of his cultural w
2 CONC ork. She returned in 1950 for just a few years back to Berlin (East). In 1954 she married the writer Arno Reinfrank.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b7/Rudolf_Feistmann%2C_Friedhof_Heerstra%C3%9Fe_-_Mutter_Erde_fec.JPG
