3 CITY New York
3 STAE New York
3 CTRY United States
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Contributed to the construction of the Jane Baerwald Aron Art Center at Mills College which was dedicated in 1986.
2 CONT
2 CONT With the dedication of the Jane Baerwald Aron Art Center, the art department faculty and gallery staff approach the new era for the visual arts at Mills with confidence and a renewed commitment to excellence. This special retrospe
2 CONC ctive exhibition of the work of Mills faculty artists is the first of an inaugural exhibition series for the 1986-87 academic year. The second exhibition of the series will be the Mills Alumnae Invitational Exhibition, a selection
2 CONC  of work by some of the many accomplished artists who received their art education at Mills College. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: http://www.mills.edu/ART/art_history.html
2 CONT ---------------------
2 CONT Natl. Assoc. Social Workers (NASW) Foundation National Programs Jane B. Aron Doctoral Fellowship
2 CONT
2 CONT The Jane Baerwald Aron Doctoral Fellowship Program provides partial support to doctoral students who are engaged in dissertation research in health care policy and practice. The fellowship program was established in 1987 as a trib
2 CONC ute to Aron, who was a leader in health care policy and education. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Jane B. Aron, who died in 1983, devoted her career to creating social policy that was responsive to people's needs. She was best known through her longtime association with New York's Mount Sinai Medical Center and Mills College i
2 CONC n California.
